Arktos Mobile changelog
=======================

Two-file convention: this file is the source of truth for release
notes; `app/src/main/assets/changelog.html` renders the same entries
inside the app (Settings → About → Changelog, or arktos://changelog).
When you add an entry here, mirror it in the HTML page.

1.2.7 — Mobile sync (MSYNC02–10)

- The desktop sync engine is ported into arktos-core: the op-log
  CRDT layer, Noise XX handshake, pairing state machine and the
  transport abstraction — behind thin compat shims
- Pairing works end-to-end: QR or manual code, the six-word
  fingerprint confirm, member management with real revoke
  (membership cut + group-key rotation)
- Encrypted device-to-device exchange with no server: LAN (QUIC +
  mDNS, debug and release) and Tor onion-service legs (release
  gecko), each degrading honestly; the periodic worker runs a
  full round — inbound frames to import, deferred-op retries,
  outbound push to every live link
- All five stores live: bookmarks and history through the real
  adapter emit/apply paths, tab presence (Settings → Synced data
  → Remote tabs opens peers' open tabs), settings over
  SharedPreferences (allow-all minus device-local exclusions),
  and the password vault — passphrase-gated E2E, strictly opt-in
- The Synchronization screen drives it all: pair/join buttons,
  device list with fingerprints, unpair, password-sync
  enable/unlock/lock and the remote-tabs feed
- Five pre-release audit rounds hardened the lane:
  * pairing/drain race — inbound frames now route through
    pair-session claims first, so a mid-handshake worker tick can
    no longer eat Noise messages or spray op frames onto a
    session-owned link
  * the pair button bound members to a "bookmarks" scope — peers
    would have rejected every "default"-scoped op
  * transport is lazy (auto→lan→mem fallback), tears itself down
    when the last member is unpaired, and holds the Android
    multicast permission + lock that mDNS needs
  * outbound push keeps a per-link sequence cursor — established
    links carry deltas instead of the whole log
  * pair-session and pending-link maps are bounded; settings emit
    moved off the main thread onto a serialized executor
  * sync/ and profiles/ are excluded from cloud + device-transfer
    backup (the Ed25519 identity key and the materialized vault)
  * the periodic worker requires network connectivity and fires
    one immediate round the moment pairing confirms
  * fixed a release-packaging bug where every sync-era APK
    shipped a pre-sync libarktos.so — the app died at launch
    resolving uniffi exports that weren't in the packaged lib




1.2.6 — Sync foundation (MSYNC01)

- Settings gets a Synchronization section (blue sync icon) with
  device identity, a sync-status row and the paired-device list —
  the shell the pairing/transport/store-sync milestones build on
- The pair action is a staged milestone: the screen says so
  honestly rather than faking a connection

1.2.5 — GeckoView 159

- GeckoView engine bumped to 159.0.20261022150525 (was
  158.0.20261019185856) — the latest published build on
  maven.mozilla.org; the new concurrent-futures transitive dep is
  pinned in the dependency-verification metadata.
  Dependabot bumps landed: okhttp 5.5.1, palette-ktx 1.1.0,
  webkit 1.18.0, gradle wrapper 9.8.2 (published sha256), and
  rusqlite 0.41.0 + Cargo.lock.
- About → Latest available version: the update check shares the
  suggestions client's disk cache, so a stale releases list could
  linger — the request now forces a fresh fetch.
- Gradle-10 deprecation warnings cleared from the build scripts.
- New-folder dialog polished: the name field sits in a padded
  container instead of hugging the dialog edge.

1.2.4 — Downloads page fix

UI:
- Menu → Downloads opens the downloads page in a new tab instead of
  reloading the current one (which left the page blank and clobbered
  the tab you were downloading from).
- About → Latest available version reads the releases list and picks
  the highest published semver — GitHub's /releases/latest pointer
  can lag and resolve to an older tag (showed "1.2.0" while 1.2.4
  was out).
- Downloads: a native Downloads screen (system DownloadManager +
  app store) replaces the generated HTML page — real entries, Open /
  Retry per item, Clear all; works even when the store read is down.
  The integrity retry also removes the stale record, so one file no
  longer shows as several partial rows. Rows follow the
  browser UX — icon, full file name, a size + source-domain
  subtitle, and a per-row overflow menu (Open / Retry / Share file /
  Share URL / Rename / Delete).
- Downloads: a gear icon opens an browser-style Download
  Settings page — default-location display, a delete policy
  (delete from device / remove from history / ask each time), and
  a 'Manage downloads with another app' toggle that routes the
  Downloads menu to the system download-manager UI.
- Downloads list is grouped into date buckets (Today /
  Yesterday / Last 7 days / Last 30 days / Older) and each row
  shows the download time in the subtitle.
- Gecko restore: a reopened-but-empty session never painted, so
  the cold-start cover held as a dark page until a tab switch
  forced a rebind — the stale-load recovery now runs after each
  session bind and reloads the tracked URL when the restore
  produced no document.
- Status bar: an aborted/abnormal video-fullscreen exit returned
  before restoring the window flags, so the status bar stayed
  hidden until the next focus event re-applied the latched flags —
  the restore now runs before the early exit. (The 'Hide status
  bar while browsing' toggle already exists under Customize.)
- Status bar readability (Android 15): enforced edge-to-edge
  drew the page under the transparent bar so icons floated over
  content only faintly scrimmed — the root view now pads by the
  status-bar inset and icon contrast follows the theme, so the
  bar reads like stock. Drops to zero in video fullscreen and
  when 'Hide status bar' is on. (Pre-Android-15 devices already
  reserve the bar area via the decor — the pad only applies on
  35+, so no empty band appears there.)
- Status bar band (all Androids): stacked fitsSystemWindows on
  the coordinator/drawer/toolbar consumed the bar inset again
  below the decor-reserved area, leaving an empty strip under the
  icons — removed from the content chain; the drawer rows'
  fitsSystemWindows went too (same double-consumption at the tab
  drawer's top). Settings pads its toolbar by the bar inset on
  API 35+, fixing the clipped title.
- History screen restyled to match Downloads: date
  buckets (Today / Yesterday / Last 7 days / Last 30 days /
  Older), a host + visit-time subtitle, and the same toolbar
  status-bar pad on Android 15+ — the Downloads and Download
  Settings toolbars get the pad too.
  History reworked again : per-day date headers,
  a letter tile per host, single-line title and URL, a per-row
  delete button, and a toolbar trash icon for clear-all. Row
  subtitles stay on one line now (the host no longer wraps
  mid-bullet). Toolbar pads moved to the parent layout — padding
  inside a fixed-height toolbar clipped the title.
  Recently closed tabs now appear at the top (recorded on tab
  delete), the toolbar trash opens a 'Time range to delete'
  dialog (last hour / today+yesterday / everything), and the
  dialog text is history-specific now — it no longer says
  'Clear downloads list'.
  Bookmark folders are now real entities: a new bookmark_folder
  table in the Rust store supports standalone/empty folders — the
  drawer's new-folder button calls it directly instead of the
  placeholder-entry workaround. Rename/delete and the folder list
  keep unioning derived names, so old folders still work.
- New-folder dialog polish: the name field now sits in a padded
  container instead of hugging the dialog's left edge.
- System-bar insets finished: the browser root now also pads by
  the nav-bar inset on Android 15+, so the bottom home/add-tab/
  back row is no longer under the virtual buttons.
- History: time-range dialog rebuilt to match the reference layout (subtitle
  + padded radio rows); history entries open a new tab via the
  shared intent path.
- Downloads page: entries were never recorded when the download-meta
  persist threw ahead of the list write — the list is now populated;
  each item gets a Retry row (re-navigates to the source URL) and a
  Clear downloads list action at the top; an empty list shows a
  proper empty state instead of a blank page. A failing store read
  also degrades to the empty state instead of a blank tab.
- Gecko autofill: browser.formfill.enable and
  extensions.formautofill.heuristics.enabled stay enabled outside
  incognito — the Save-passwords toggle only gates the signon
  save/fill pipeline. The GeckoView itself is now also marked
  importantForAutofill — geckoview-158's setAutofillEnabled never
  did that, so Android's autofill framework skipped the view
  entirely (Bitwarden saw no fields, no context-menu entry).
- Downloads: the post-completion integrity retry deleted the
  finished file BEFORE re-enqueueing — a failed re-queue (expired
  signed URL) left no file and a dead notification. The partial is
  now only dropped once a retry is actually in flight. The download
  request's MIME also falls back to the file extension when the
  server reports octet-stream, so the finished-download notification
  actually opens the file (installer for APKs).
- Gecko restore: an upgrade could "reproduce" an empty SessionState
  and commit about:blank, which overwrote the tracked URL — the
  first tab then reloaded the blank and lost its title. Blank
  commits before any real document no longer clobber the tracked
  URL, so recovery reloads the real page. A generated-page load can
  also arrive before the session opens (silent drop → untitled empty
  tab) — loads now open the session first. The list read also has a
  3s timeout — a wedged store call left the tab blank forever
  instead of degrading to the empty state; the whole build chain is
  bounded too, with a written fallback page so something always
  renders.
- Settings: pad the fragment container by the navigation-bar inset —
  the last rows of Settings screens (Customization, General, …) sat
  under the system nav bar in edge-to-edge mode.


1.2.3 — Download dialog crash fix

Engine:
- TapjackingGuard no longer crashes on OEMs that deny
  HIDE_OVERLAY_WINDOWS (SecurityException on download dialogs,
  both engines; confirmed by a field dump via Share crash log).


1.2.2 — Fullscreen crash fix

Engine:
- Gecko fullscreen (HTML5 video) no longer kills the app: entering
  fullscreen on a session whose view can't be cleanly reparented or
  rebound threw an IllegalStateException through GeckoView's
  delegate; the fullscreen entry is now guarded (declines instead of
  crashing) and the shell's fullscreen reparent only adds a detached
  view. Confirmed by a field crash dump (1.2.1's Share crash log).


1.2.1 — Download crash fix + crash log sharing

Engine:
- Download pipeline hardened on both engines: download callbacks
  re-dispatch to the main thread, a destroyed host activity drops
  the request instead of dying on a stale window token, and the
  confirm/risk dialogs degrade gracefully when the window cannot be
  shown — fixes the crash when tapping an asset link (e.g. a release
  APK on github.com).
- Settings → About → Share crash log sends the newest recorded crash
  dump through the system share sheet (no manual file browsing).
- Dependency bump: ctutils 0.4.3 → 0.4.6 (RUSTSEC-2026-0385).
- Regression test for the download filename/Content-Disposition path
  (DownloadCrashReproTest).


1.2 — Passwords

Engine:
- Saved-password support on both engines: submitting a login now
  offers a "Save password?" prompt, saved credentials autofill on
  revisit (single match fills directly, multiple accounts get a
  chooser), and clearing form/all web data wipes the store.
  - Gecko ("full"): GeckoView stores no logins itself, so the app
    provides the Autocomplete.StorageDelegate + login prompt plumbing
    (onLoginSave/onLoginSelect) this requires.
  - WebView ("light"): importantForAutofill only talks to external
    autofill services, so a postMessage login bridge now captures
    submitted credentials and injects saved ones into login forms.
  (AUTOF02)
- Logins persist encrypted at rest (Android Keystore–wrapped AES-GCM
  file under the app's private dir), never in private-mode sessions:
  the incognito runtime gets no storage delegate/login bridge and
  signon prefs are switched off there.
- The "Save passwords" privacy toggle gates the save prompt
  (signon.rememberSignons); the 1.1 system-autofill integration
  stays active alongside for devices with an autofill service
  configured.


1.1 — Stability & maintenance release

Engine:
- GeckoView pinned to the stable release channel
  (org.mozilla.geckoview:geckoview — the unsuffixed artifact is the
  stable line; -beta/-nightly are not used). The 158.0.2 bump was
  reverted to the verified 158.0.1 build after it regressed
  background-tab restore; the pin moves forward once a newer
  stable verifies clean.
- Restore recovery no longer trusts engine flags alone: stop()
  arms its own abort signal and a committed document clears it,
  so a tab whose load was killed without a callback still
  recovers on select.
- Tab titles persist in saved state and are reapplied on
  restore (TITLE_KEY + Page.restoreTitle), so the tab strip
  shows the page name before its reload commits — the parity
  the WebView backend gets for free from saved history.
- Gecko video fullscreen follows the Fenix model: gecko renders
  the fullscreen element inside the existing view, so the shell
  hides chrome (toolbar + system bars, toolbar-offset
  translation) instead of reparenting — fixes the "child already
  has a parent" crash, the whitespace/truncation, and restores
  correctly on exit.
- Update check (UPDT01): a daily GitHub Releases lookup (opt-out
  in General settings; incognito never checks) announces a newer
  tag once via dialog — "Download" opens the release page.

Privacy & permissions:
- Site-permission grants are now covered by the engine StorageArea
  model (SitePermissions): clearing web storage wipes remembered
  geolocation/notification/autoplay/camera/mic decisions on both
  engines — GeckoView's SharedPreferences store and the WebView
  GeolocationPermissions database — instead of leaving them behind.
- New "Site permissions" row in Privacy settings lists every stored
  per-origin grant with per-origin removal and a clear-all action.

Networking:
- Cleartext/network-security audit: plain HTTP remains permitted
  (a browser must load http:// sites) but the manifest
  networkSecurityConfig now documents the policy and the
  Force-HTTPS warning path covers the risk.

Persistence & restore:
- Tab restore no longer trusts the engine SessionState parcel as
  the source of truth — the plain URL list is authoritative and
  engine state is applied opportunistically on top, so an
  engine-upgrade-incompatible bundle can never white-screen a tab.
- Regression tests cover the save→kill→restore path: aborted
  background restores re-issue their URL instead of staying blank.

Architecture & modernization:
- Tab-view swapping and fullscreen plumbing extracted from
  BrowserActivity (2,700+ lines) into a dedicated controller —
  smaller blast radius for future display/tab changes.
- Deprecated-API sweep: typed getParcelable calls, modern
  display-metrics lookup, OnBackPressedDispatcher, and the
  Activity Result API replace the deprecated surfaces lint flags.
- Adblock subscription staleness verified — lists refresh on the
  documented cadence instead of shipping stale.
- Android Autofill framework integration so system password
  managers can fill and save through the browser: the WebView
  flavor opts the view into autofill, and the Gecko flavor rides
  GeckoView's built-in AndroidAutofillDelegate — disabled on
  incognito pages on both engines so private sessions neither
  fill nor save.

1.0 — Arktos Mobile: first release
Rebrand / project:
- Rebranded the project from SmartCookieWeb to Arktos Mobile: package
  com.cookiegames.smartcookie → com.arktosbrowser.mobile, Arktos logo
  icon set in every density and flavor, dead hosted services replaced
  with neutral defaults (translate/news endpoints emptied, upstream
  suggestion + SearX endpoints removed), and every user-visible string,
  README, ONLINE doc and fastlane metadata now says Arktos (REBRAND01).
- Residual SmartCookie* identifiers renamed to ArktosCookie*
  (SmartCookieView → ArktosCookieView, SmartCookieWebClient →
  ArktosCookieWebClient, SmartCookieChromeClient →
  ArktosCookieChromeClient, SmartCookieViewTitle →
  ArktosCookieViewTitle); upstream project-name citations kept as
  attribution (RENAM01).
- Engine-coupling audit groundwork: engine/BrowserEngine.kt boundary
  sketch plus .devin/ENGINE.md + check-engine-audit.sh tracking every
  android.webkit touchpoint for a possible future selectable-engine
  effort (ENG01).
- LIMITATIONS.md documents the upstream issues that are Android
  WebView platform limits rather than fixable bugs (DOCS01).

Rust core:
- New rust/ workspace with an arktos-core cdylib exposed to Kotlin
  through UniFFI; Gradle cross-compiles per-ABI jniLibs via cargo-ndk
  and generates the Kotlin bindings at build time (RCORE01).
- BlocklistEngine in Rust unifies ad/malware/site-block/LAN verdicts —
  one call per shouldInterceptRequest; hosts-file parsing moved to
  Rust; public-page→private-network requests blocked behind a privacy
  toggle (BLOCK01).
- ArktosStore (rusqlite) replaces the five SQLiteOpenHelper databases
  behind unchanged repository interfaces; Netscape bookmark import
  uses a Rust HTML tokenizer (STORE01).
- Search suggestions, userscript metadata/@include parsing, download
  filename rules, bookmark JSON import/export and reader-mode
  extraction (dom_smoothie) all run in the Rust core; matching Kotlin
  models and helpers deleted (PORT01).
- URL utilities, error/block page builders, color math and the
  app-lock/parental password hashing (argon2id, in-place upgrade of
  legacy plaintext entries) ported to Rust in a second sweep (PORT02).
- Multi-list adblock subscriptions mirroring the desktop preset
  catalog, with per-list toggles, custom URL/file lists, staleness
  refresh and a privacy-settings screen managing them (LIST01,
  PREFS01).
- Tranco + Majestic site-rank lists merge a vendored seed with
  downloaded drop files through a streaming Rust parser, consent-gated
  behind the same privacy screen (RANK01).
- ArktosStore schema v3 adds run_at/no_frames userscript columns and a
  gm_value table backing GM_*Value persistence (STORE02).

Web-view fixes (upstream SmartCookieWeb issues):
- Error/interstitial pages got a stable non-null baseUrl
  (https://arktos-error.local) instead of loading with a null base
  under JavaScript enabled (upstream PR #329 for #328; FIXA02).
- StartPage search moved off the retired startpage.com/do/* endpoints
  to www.startpage.com/sp/search (#326; FIXA01).
- AMOLED theme: the active tab in the drawer now has a visible
  selection contrast against the black background (#298; FIXA03).
- The URL bar can trim protocol/www for display only — the loaded
  URL is untouched (#278; FIXA04).
- Certificate info dialog stays fully reachable at maximum system
  font/display scaling (#277; FIXA05).
- Text zoom ceiling raised to 400% while keeping the original
  25–200% steps and default (#275; FIXA06).
- New 'Follow system' theme option flips the browser theme and the
  dark-web addon with the system night mode; manual override still
  wins (#251; FIXA07).
- One-tap new-tab button in the toolbar while tabs live in the drawer
  (#299; FIXA08), plus an option to swap the tabs/bookmarks drawer
  icon positions (#297; FIXA09).
- Downloads verify completeness and retry truncated or retryable
  failures, resolve real filenames from Content-Disposition/mime type
  instead of falling back to .bin, and warn when a server returns HTML
  for a file download (#270/#311/#303; FIXB01).
- Error pages no longer persist their data: URI as the tab's URL —
  the original address survives restarts and undo-close (#281; FIXB02).
- First tapped link or pasted URL after returning to the app is no
  longer eaten by a mid-navigation user-agent rewrite (#309; FIXB03).
- SSL warnings are gated to one prompt per page load instead of a
  dialog loop that could freeze the app (#296; FIXB04).
- App links prefer installed handler apps over the Play Store, honour
  browser_fallback_url, and can no longer loop back into the browser
  itself (#316; FIXB05).
- target=_blank links no longer crash on undeliverable popup
  transports — the window request is declined and the link loads in
  the current tab (#306; FIXB06).
- A mistyped app-lock password keeps the prompt open with an error
  instead of killing the app (#302; FIXB07).
- Per-site JavaScript/cookie quick-toggles from the page menu and the
  long-press link dialog, overriding the global setting per origin
  (#305; FIXB09).
- A dedicated 'No internet connection' page replaces the generic
  error when the device is offline; reload retries the real URL
  (#323; FIXB10).
- Forced SafeSearch across Google/Bing/DuckDuckGo/Yandex behind the
  password-gated parental-control setting survives URL-bar edits,
  bookmarks and redirects (#327; FIXB11).
- Page translation rebuilt on a LibreTranslate-compatible endpoint
  (configurable, default libretranslate.de) with the wire format in
  Rust and an on-demand JS bridge — the dead Microsoft translator
  path is gone (#300; FIXB12).
- WebView hardening pass: intent-scheme allowlist on incoming VIEW
  intents, no user-CA trust, no cloud backup, download filename
  sanitization and dead-code removal (SECFIX).
- WebView Safe Browsing channel disabled outright; reader-mode page
  failures and proxy bypass leaks fixed (SECFIX02).
- Userscript engine rebuilt on WebViewCompat document-start injection
  plus a web-message GM bridge — @run-at/@exclude/@include/@require
  honoured, @require fetched once via the proxy-aware OkHttp client,
  GM_xmlhttpRequest/GM_setClipboard/GM_openInTab and the GM.* promise
  API implemented, GM_*Value persisted to the Rust store; legacy
  evaluation kept as a fallback for old WebViews (USENG01).

UI:
- Error/block interstitials restyled to the Arktos desktop look —
  centered card, gradient header band, floated logo, hint list and
  pill buttons, emitted by the Rust page builders with an arktos-dark
  variant (UI01).
- Start and incognito pages restyled to the Arktos desktop startpage —
  aurora-wave hero, cresting logo and gradient header; the redundant
  in-page search box removed; customizable link tiles kept (UI02).
- In-app changelog page (this document) reachable from
  Settings → About → Changelog and via arktos://changelog; after an
  upgrade the changelog opens once in a new tab (CHLOG01).
- Arktos light/dark brand themes added to the theme picker, including
  'Follow system' resolution to the Arktos variants (THEME01).
- Desktop-parity site shield before the URL bar opens a per-site
  privacy panel (ad-block, JS, cookies, SafeSearch overrides); the
  padlock is tinted by the site's shield verdict (SHIELD01).
- Bookmark rows resolve real favicons straight from the host —
  declared link icons then /favicon.ico, with ICO-container decoding,
  a SHA-256-keyed disk cache and a 30-day TTL; no third-party icon
  service (ICON01).
- Tabs drawer gained a header X offering close-all / close-others;
  closing the last tab now always leaves a fresh default tab instead
  of exiting, saved-tab restore order is deterministic again, and a
  corrupt saved session can't leave the browser tab-less (TABS01).
- The logo overflow menu hardened: rows that need a page hide when
  none is loaded, null-tab crashes eliminated, dark-theme background
  restored, and a 'Close browser' action added under Settings
  (MENU01).

Build / housekeeping:
- Build fixed for JDK 21 (jacoco bump, locale string fixes);
  jetifier dropped; dead dependencies replaced (BOOT01).
- Upstream housekeeping decisions recorded: own icon set (#168 N/A),
  GitHub Releases + in-repo fastlane metadata as the F-Droid
  prerequisite (#314), 'userscript' and manual-proxy support
  documented (#315/#325; HOUSE01).
- RxJava 2 → 3 migration, targetSdk 35 / minSdk 26 bump, ButterKnife
  and netcipher dropped, deprecated news feed removed, Naver search
  engine retired, quick-start tiles pointed at Arktos destinations
  (HOUSE02).

Settings audit (every screen verified end-to-end):
- Advanced: dead "integrated download manager" switch wired to a real
  third-party hand-off, SHIFT_JIS label corrected, dev-tools row
  crash-proofed, translation-endpoint summary fixed (SETA01).
- Import/export moved fully to the Storage Access Framework (the old
  runtime permission gate fails on targetSdk 35), settings backup now
  a typed JSON-lines round-trip that parses before wiping, bookmark
  format detected by content not MIME type, and tab backup/restore
  implemented through the live browser activity (SETA02).
- Customization/Privacy: homepage-type row tracks changes live, dead
  bindings removed, manual-proxy choice only persists after host/port
  validation, "Save form data" labelled correctly, destructive clears
  confirm first and can't crash (SETA03).
- General: download location must be writable to persist, custom
  search only commits after a valid https:// template, mis-tagged
  placeholder requirements corrected (SETA04).
- Parental controls: shared no-password flag that could hard-lock the
  section removed, every password field now masks input, retry no
  longer stacks dialogs (SETA05).

Security:
- Browser-wide app lock: choose PIN, password, or biometric unlock in
  Settings → Privacy; re-lock timing configurable (immediately,
  1/5/10 minutes, or a custom minute count) driven by a monotonic
  background clock — the gate re-arms on cold start and after the
  window elapses (SEC01).
- Encrypted backup: Settings → Import/Export gains password-protected
  backup archives (PBKDF2 → AES-256-GCM, versioned ARKBAK format)
  covering bookmarks + settings, restorable only with the password.
  Auto Backup's database inclusion was removed at the same time so
  history/bookmarks/downloads no longer ship to the cloud in
  plaintext (SEC02).

Search suggestions:
- Provider list rebuilt: Baidu (HTTP-only, GBK wire format) and Naver
  removed; Startpage (OpenSearch JSON via www.startpage.com/
  osuggestions) and Qwant (api.qwant.com/v3/suggest) added — all
  remaining providers are HTTPS (SUGG01).
- New installs default to DuckDuckGo; stored choices for removed
  providers migrate to DuckDuckGo rather than silently switching to
  Google (SUGG01).
- Qwant suggestion requests carry the device locale
  (language_COUNTRY, e.g. de_DE, pt-BR → pt_BR) instead of a
  hardcoded en_US; unknown locales fall back to en_US (SUGG02).

Security (continued):
- Mixed content is blocked by default in normal browsing (SEC03);
  Force HTTPS now warns on cleartext navigations instead of silently
  upgrading, with upgrade/back/proceed choices (SEC04).
- The in-page translation bridge exposes only a postMessage surface
  to web pages (SEC05); the userscript GM bridge enforces @connect
  domains and origin gating (SEC06).
- Incognito windows are FLAG_SECURE — no screenshots or recents
  thumbnails — and an optional whole-app secure-window toggle exists
  (SEC07); sensitive dialogs filter overlay touches to block
  tapjacking (SEC08).
- Exported components and incoming VIEW intents were audited and
  hardened, and the external panic TRIGGER intent sits behind a
  privacy toggle (SEC09); release builds shrink resources with R8
  keep rules for the Rust bridge (SEC10).
- Downloads warn before enqueueing executables or disguised file
  types (SEC11); internationalized domains display as punycode in
  the URL bar so lookalikes stand out (SEC12); a privacy toggle
  trims referrers on top-level navigations (SEC13).
- CI gates check dependency integrity, committed secrets and the
  manifest surface (SEC14); the browsing database encrypts at rest
  via SQLCipher (SEC15); toolchains are pinned and dependencies
  verified for reproducible builds (SEC16 — see REPRODUCIBLE.md).
- Navigations send DNT: 1 and Sec-GPC: 1 on main-frame GETs (SEC17);
  the header re-issue path is GET-only so POST bodies are no longer
  corrupted, and WebView's subresource header gap is documented in
  ONLINE.md.
- The app-lock prompt is a full-screen lock screen — PIN, password
  or biometric — covering the whole browser including tabs.

Dual engine (ENG02–ENG05):
- engine/BrowserEngine.kt grew into a real Backend/Profile/Page
  seam; the WebView implementation moved behind it as the webview
  flavor backend (ENG02).
- Product flavors split the build: scMainWebview ships as
  "Arktos Light" (com.arktosbrowser.mobile) and scMainGecko as
  "Arktos" (com.arktosbrowser.mobile.full, arm64-only release)
  (ENG03).
- Gecko parity pass A: navigation decisions, request policy, SSL
  errors, tab state and prompts/downloads run on GeckoView
  delegates (ENG04).
- Gecko parity pass B: storage/cookies, proxy/I2P plumbing,
  userscript injection and capability-gated settings (ENG05).
- The Page interface exposes desktop-mode UA toggling on both
  engines.

Incognito hardening:
- The incognito WebView partition is wiped when the session ends and
  on every fresh start, so cookies and logins cannot carry between
  private sessions (INCOG01); panic clean covers the incognito
  profile too (INCOG02).
- The private-tabs reminder notification hides from the lock screen
  (INCOG03); the incognito URL bar opts out of keyboard personalized
  learning (INCOG04).

Modernization sweep (MOD01–MOD10):
- Download entry points, ReadingActivity and Utils.kt moved off
  deprecated APIs; camera uploads use FileProvider URIs instead of
  raw file:// (MOD01–MOD03).
- Dead PreferenceActivity wrappers deleted; file picking, adblock
  host import and the I2P launch migrated to Activity Result APIs;
  the callback/reflection PermissionsManager was replaced by a
  single RequestMultiplePermissions launcher (MOD04–MOD06).
- The horizontal/vertical tab-list animators merged into one
  ArktosItemAnimator; overridePendingTransition calls moved to
  overrideActivityTransition on API 34+; AnimatedProgressBar
  slimmed to a single retargeted animator and J2K-era null handling
  cleaned up in the remaining helpers (MOD07–MOD10).

Naming / docs:
- The WebView flavor installs as "Arktos Light" and the GeckoView
  flavor as "Arktos"; the in-app name follows the flavor via
  resValue.
- ONLINE.md and README were corrected so online-service claims match
  actual defaults (suggestions on via DuckDuckGo, news feed removed,
  translation endpoint pre-set but feature off).
- Repo-wide SPDX headers now read "Copyright 2014 A.C.R. and Arktos
  contributors", keeping upstream attribution.


Dependency updates (v1.0):
- Kotlin 2.4.0 → 2.4.21; Compose compiler 2.4.20 → 2.4.21; KSP
  2.3.4 → 2.3.12.
- Gradle wrapper 9.6.0 → 9.8.1 (jar, scripts and distribution
  checksum all updated and verified).
- jsoup 1.22.2 → 1.23.2, fixing the HTML-sanitizer CVEs flagged by
  the OSV scan (GHSA-65r4-943x-97jj, GHSA-pmhh-3w7g-xqp8).
- org.json 20250517 → 20260814 (unit-test JVM only).
- argon2 0.5.x → 0.6.0 in the Rust core; the password-hashing code
  was adapted to the new API (internal salt generation, the
  SaltString/rand_core pair dropped). 145/145 Rust tests green.
- rusqlite 0.40.1 → 0.40.2, aho-corasick 1.1.3 → 1.1.5 and
  miniz_oxide 0.8.x → 0.9.1 in Cargo.lock.
- CI: actions/setup-java v5 → v6; the Rust toolchain step now pins
  1.99.0 plus the three Android targets explicitly; the OSV scan
  runs the real nested action and is scoped to rust/ so build-time
  Gradle tooling is no longer mis-flagged; dependency-verification
  metadata regenerated to cover the previously-missing BOM modules.

Gecko engine hardening (v1.0 maintenance):
- Tab switching reworked around one shared GeckoView — the
  mozilla-components EngineView model — binding and unbinding
  sessions in place. Per-tab GeckoViews lost their compositor
  surface on detach/reattach and painted black.
- ArktosGeckoView releases its session before any window detach so
  GeckoView can't auto-close it — the root cause of dead/frozen tabs
  when swapping to WebView-backed pages (homepage, bookmarks) or
  entering fullscreen; the pending session re-binds on re-attach.
- Killed content processes recover: GeckoView reports process kills
  via onKill (not onCrash); dead sessions re-open and re-apply their
  SessionState on next select — immediately for the foreground tab —
  and setSession never binds a closed session.
- Tab restore hardened end to end: saved bundles unparcel with the
  app classloader, every saved tab carries a URL fallback, a plain
  URL list restores tabs when the parcel itself is unreadable, and a
  bad per-tab bundle drops only that tab instead of the whole
  restore. Engine state restores ahead of the URL fallback so scroll
  and history survive.
- Restored background tabs no longer come back empty: the intended
  URL is tracked eagerly (WebView getUrl() parity) and loads aborted
  by the post-initialization stop() are re-issued on select.
- Site permission decisions (geolocation, notifications, autoplay,
  camera/mic) are remembered per origin — persisted for regular tabs,
  memory-only in incognito — so prompts stop repeating on every tab
  switch and restart.
- Generated chrome pages on gecko: arktos://changelog and bundled
  file:// pages serve their HTML as data loads with artwork inlined
  as data URIs, intercepted before navigation so the pipeline can't
  stall; window.close() maps to tab close (WebView parity) and
  fullscreen exit re-attaches the shared view.
- Startup fix: BrowserApp runs engine init only in browser processes —
  GeckoView's ~10 child service processes (crashhelper, gpu, tab,
  media) no longer race the main profile and kill the launch.
- Text reflow on gecko rides the bundled userscript WebExtension —
  element-tagging reflow driven by visualViewport with a live toggle
  (no reload needed); font-inflation double-apply removed.
- Search defaults: DuckDuckGo is the default engine and the default
  suggestions provider.
